            "simpleExplanation": "可以 (kěyǐ) means \"can\" or \"may.\" Use it to ask permission to do something: put 可以 before the verb, and add 吗 at the end to make it a question — 我可以坐这儿吗? = \"Can I sit here?\" To say yes, just answer 可以 (You may); to say no, say 不可以 (You may not).",
            "visualExamples": [
              {
                "script": "我可以坐这儿吗?",
                "romanization": "Wǒ kěyǐ zuò zhèr ma?",
                "english": "Can I sit here?"
              },
              {
                "script": "可以。",
                "romanization": "Kěyǐ.",
                "english": "Sure, you may.",
                "note": "可以 on its own is a simple 'yes, you may'"
              },
              {
                "script": "我可以坐在你旁边吗?",
                "romanization": "Wǒ kěyǐ zuò zài nǐ pángbiān ma?",
                "english": "Can I sit next to you?",
                "note": "可以 + verb + 吗 = asking permission to do anything"
              }
            ],
            "difficulty": 2,
            "quiz": [
